From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruiyangke <me@ry.ke>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gpui_ios: One iPad window per window, edge to edge

gpui_ios supported one connected scene and laid a window out inside the
system's safe area, so a second window was refused and the layout never
reached the display's edges or knew about iPadOS 26's window controls.

Each normal window gets a UIKit scene (an iPad window) of its own, opened from
the one in use so Stage Manager puts it beside that one. Application state
tracks every scene: foreground and active state aggregate across them, a
disconnected scene's windows return to that session's next scene, and
closing the last window of a scene closes it. Sessions iPadOS keeps for
windows a killed run left behind are reused before a new one is requested,
because iPadOS can't close them while they have no scene; a session that
belongs to a window the app hid is left alone. An iPad window the
person closes asks its windows to close, and a window the app keeps (unsaved
work) gets an iPad window again. `set_next_window_role` tells the next window
which app it belongs to (its title and subtitle in the App Switcher), whether
it is a sheet over a parent (modal or not, movable by its bar), and the sizes
its iPad window may take. A window bar draws the title beside the window
controls, with a Close menu and Paste for when iPadOS shows none.

A window is laid out edge to edge, as iPadOS's own apps are: GPUI draws under
the status bar and the home indicator and reads them as safe area insets.
`WindowInsets::window_controls` is the room the system's window controls take
at the top-leading corner, so an app draws its title bar beside them; it
follows the controls as they appear and move. The keyboard's overlap is
measured per window, so another scene's keyboard doesn't move this one. The
status bar style is `None` (follows the appearance), light or dark, and a
window with a bar follows the system's. Touch and hold is the secondary
click, two fingers pinch and pan, and a trackpad's or mouse's pointer over
the window hovers (`is_hovered`, hover status, mouse move and exit events).

Remove when upstream gpui_ios supports several windows and reports the window
controls.
